# C. elegans mitochondrial nucleotide composition

This lesson ports the deterministic, real-sequence portion of Exercise 1.8 from [Modern Statistics for Modern Biology](https://www.huber.embl.de/msmb/01-chap.html). It uses the same UCSC `ce2` chromosome M assembly as the source's `BSgenome.Celegans.UCSC.ce2` object.

```biolang
let ucsc = read_json("data/ucsc-ce2-chrM.json")
let chromosome_m = dna(ucsc.dna)
let observed = base_counts(chromosome_m)
{
    assembly: ucsc.genome,
    chromosome: ucsc.chrom,
    length: len(chromosome_m),
    counts: observed
}
```

The source reports `A=4335`, `C=1225`, `G=2055`, and `T=6179` for 13,794 nucleotides.

```biolang
let total = observed.A + observed.C + observed.G + observed.T
let expected = total / 4.0
let observed_equal =
    (observed.A - expected) * (observed.A - expected) / expected +
    (observed.C - expected) * (observed.C - expected) / expected +
    (observed.G - expected) * (observed.G - expected) / expected +
    (observed.T - expected) * (observed.T - expected) / expected
{
    proportions: {
        A: observed.A / total,
        C: observed.C / total,
        G: observed.G / total,
        T: observed.T / total
    },
    equal_expected_count: expected,
    observed_equal_statistic: observed_equal
}
```

The later random multinomial simulation is not included, so this lesson creates no synthetic sequence or synthetic count table. This exercise section publishes numeric output rather than a canonical figure.

```biolang
assert len(chromosome_m) == 13794, "published mitochondrial length"
assert observed.A == 4335, "published A count"
assert observed.C == 1225, "published C count"
assert observed.G == 2055, "published G count"
assert observed.T == 6179, "published T count"
assert total == 13794, "published total"
assert abs(expected - 3448.5) < 0.000000001, "published equal-frequency expectation"
assert abs(observed_equal - 4386.633898796578) < 0.000001, "published observed-equal statistic"
"Exact UCSC sequence and source composition outputs verified."
```
